    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1924-09-02; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Tired but well; temperature 37.4 °C, pulse 90, blood pressure 120/76, oxygen saturation 97% on room air, respirations 16</td></tr><tr><td>Ears, nose, mouth, and throat</td><td>Red throat without exudate; no mouth ulcers or thrush; clear nasal discharge</td></tr><tr><td>Neck</td><td>No tender or enlarged lymph nodes</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Clear to auscultation bilaterally; no crackles or wheeze; oxygen saturation stays at 97% after walking the corridor</td></tr><tr><td>Skin</td><td>Port site clean, without redness or tenderness; no rash</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

